{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00488 - MONDO_16249",
  "verbalization": "Altretamine, through its indication for Ovarian Adenocarcinoma and Malignant Dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor of Ovary, is linked to Cisplatin, which in turn is associated with Hereditary Site-specific Ovarian Cancer Syndrome. This suggests a potential pathway where Altretamine may influence the development or progression of ovarian cancer, which is a known precursor to Hereditary Site-specific Ovarian Cancer Syndrome. The shared use of Cisplatin in these contexts implies a possible mechanism involving chemotherapy or targeted therapy, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence points to a possible dependency on cisplatin for the development of the syndrome, but further research is needed to establish a direct causal link. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of chemotherapy in the pathogenesis of ovarian cancer and its potential impact on hereditary forms of the disease.",
